i'm dave rubin and i'm host of the  reuben report a show where i try to have  reasonably informed conversations about  politics  we're all about to sit around the table  for thanksgiving with our loved ones at  one of the most divisive periods in  american history  there are some of you who don't want to  see your relatives or have disinvited  them due to disagreements about politics  and that's why it's more important than  ever to resist the urge to assume the  worst intentions  in our family and in our friends if  you're a democrat or a left-leaning type  don't assume that because your relative  voted for trump or is a republican that  they are a racist homophobic bigot  their reasons for thinking the way they  do may be more nuanced and complex than  you may think  if you're a trump voting republican  don't assume that your  liberal relatives are all socialists  wanting to throw out the constitution  there are sane liberals who are not  radical and don't align with the burn it  all down lefty crowd  there aren't many of those liberals left  but that makes it all the more important  to find them  and talk to them it's important to  understand and not forget that we  actually want  a lot of the same things we want to have  successful lives for us and our children  and others but we have different ideas  on how we can get there  what i do know is that we won't get  there by cutting people  out of our lives and making the walls of  our echo chambers taller  than they already are so you don't have  to agree with my politics or who i voted  for  but if you agree that we can only get to  a better world by trying to better  understand each other  not by ostracizing each other then share  this video  if you think it's a better idea to  assume the best in our opponents instead  of the worst  then share this video share it with  someone you're worried about getting  into a fight with  at thanksgiving share it with people you  know that you agree with  and share it with those who don't we can  only fix society's problems by working  together and trying to better understand  each other  so if you only agree with that message  alone share this so we can all get on  the same page  to start rebuilding the bridges we've  been so busy burning  all right now more importantly than any  of that get off social media  get hopped up on tryptophan and take a  nap  happy thanksgiving everybody if you're  looking for more honest and thoughtful  conversations about politics instead of  non-stop yelling check out our politics  playlist and if you want to watch full  interviews on a variety of topics watch  our full episode playlist  all right over here and to get notified  of all future videos be sure to  subscribe and click the notification  bell
 

